      "created_at": "2014-05-09T11:22:28.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The only time you can lose \"nothing\" of something to avoid/trigger an effect is discarding your hand when you have zero cards, because a hand of zero cards is still a hand (Toxic Seaweed in Atlantis is an example of this). Otherwise, you must always discard/destroy the specified number of cards in order to achieve whatever it is.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:30:19.013Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
